<title>USA: OXiGENE rises on report.</title>
<headline>OXiGENE rises on report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in cancer drug company OXiGENE Inc rose on Tuesday after a favorable report from Swedish broker Carnegie.</p>
<p>The company's stock were up 2-1/2 to 30-1/2 after hitting 31-3/4 in morning trade. Volume was heavy at 185,100 shares.</p>
<p>Although a company spokeswoman said she knew no reason for the rise, it followed the report by Carnegie. Details were not immediately available, and the spokeswoman said the analysis probably would be made available on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The company debuted on the Stockholm exchange in November.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
